_ext('ground-floor-garage', [
  {'t': 'p', 'text': 'If your building has shared parking or storage, tell the manager at once. Water that moves between levels affects neighbors, and early notice gets pumps, drain checks and shared records moving while the event is still small.'},
  {'t': 'p', 'text': 'Ask the crew to note the high-water line on walls and posts before cleanup begins. That mark shows how deep the water reached and helps decide how far materials must be removed.'}])

_ext('mold-removal-services', [
  {'t': 'p', 'text': 'Keep all paperwork from the job in one folder: the written scope, photos before and after, drying records and any test reports. If you sell or refinance later, that file answers most of the questions a buyer or lender is likely to ask.'},
  {'t': 'p', 'text': 'Finally, plan for the rebuild. Removal leaves open walls or missing drywall, and the repair crew needs a dry, cleared space. Ask each company whether it handles the rebuild or hands it off, and how the schedule will fit together.'}])

_ext('what-kills-mold-marina', [
  {'t': 'p', 'text': 'If a spot keeps coming back in the same place after you have cleaned and dried it, treat that as information. Something is feeding it, whether a slow leak, a cold wall or trapped humidity, and a moisture meter will find it faster than another round of cleaner.'}])

_ext('what-kills-black-mold', [
  {'t': 'h2', 'text': 'A realistic timeline for a small, contained job'},
  {'t': 'p', 'text': 'A contained job usually moves through assessment, moisture repair, setup, removal, drying and a final check. The pace depends on whether the source is found on the first visit and how long drying takes. Ask each step to be explained in plain language and ask for the schedule in writing.'},
  {'t': 'p', 'text': 'If a company offers to start within minutes with no inspection, ask what the work will include. A crew that has not seen the space cannot know the scope, and a scope that is a guess usually changes midway through the job.'},
  {'t': 'p', 'text': 'Finally, keep expectations honest. A good result is a dry building, removed or cleaned growth and a clear record of what was done. It is not a promise about the future, because moisture can always return if a new leak appears.'}])
